    <item>
      <title>Jean 0.4.5</title>
      <pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 03:13:47 GMT</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>249</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.4.5</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>13.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description>&lt;h3&gt;Jean 0.4.5&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Fixes&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Studio: in 0.4.4 every Studio message ended with no answer (Claude was started without the message). Fixed. A message typed before Studio has finished opening is now held and sent as soon as it is ready instead of being lost. The same bug stopped Settings › Keys from saving a key in 0.4.4; fixed too. (#30, #39) - Studio: a message typed early is never lost: if Studio can't open or no Claude is found, it goes back into the message box with a note. Pressing Stop just before a retry now always stops. (#40) - A specialist is never restarted to free up memory before it has written its handoff notes: Jean asks you to check on it instead. It is never started twice either. (#27) - Jean.app no longer crashes when a window closes while a command it started is being stopped. (#45) - `jean doctor` no longer tells a desktop Mac "Laptops don't have it" when it can't find the restart-after-power-failure setting. (#35)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Security&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- The guard stops forged approvals and secret reads hidden behind wildcards, braces, variables, arrays, loops, `cd`, `xargs` and similar shell forms. (#38) - The guard stops writes into its own files through 17 tricky shell forms it used to miss. (#31) - The guard matches file names in any letter case, with accents, and through links, so CAPS or a shortcut can't sneak past it. (#37) - A read-only git command redirected into Jean's own files (for example, git log written over the approvals file) now counts as a write and is stopped. (#34) - False alarm fixed: commit messages and PR text that only mention Jean's own files are no longer blocked. Real writes to those files and secret reads are still stopped. (#32)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;New&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Studio: a mic button types what you say into the message box (macOS asks for the microphone and speech recognition once), and Shift+Enter makes a new line while Enter still sends. (#36) - New setup guide page, "Your always-on Mac and restarts", and three new `jean doctor` checks: FileVault, automatic login, and restart after a power failure. (#29)&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/msiegerJBI/jean-updates/releases/download/v0.4.5/Jean.dmg" length="140832837" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="UP+4hvXKL9x7HUBwMFrbKDqmsv9/4ET//N52yV2kvSEcb/VGerbH/LAYplQXf34+atui5CJNw/eRHn5NP7xrBQ==" />
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Jean 0.4.4</title>
      <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:59:06 GMT</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>206</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.4.4</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>13.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description>&lt;h3&gt;Jean 0.4.4&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Only you approve. A specialist can no longer act as you: code it writes for a tab stays a draft until you preview and publish it (hub › To approve), and an automation it changes turns off until you approve the new steps, which the Slack message now shows in full.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Jean.app proves itself to the hub without sending its key, and the hub's sign-in for your windows lives only in memory, so nothing on this Mac can copy it.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The Library never copies a file that points somewhere else, or anything from Jean's own folder.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Slack task cards say "Waiting on you" when a specialist needs your answer, and tick off every step when the task is done.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The phone hub setup accepts Cloudflare account tokens, and says plainly when a token is mistyped.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/msiegerJBI/jean-updates/releases/download/v0.4.4/Jean.dmg" length="140845844" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="gP+uFGUBRIbW5NfGD3QyjO65o1ARxbWCFwLPLPtiNN8GFryhwoEbUnty3duY0p6IxvbgsnBhnLlCRBgU5KYXDA==" />
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Jean 0.4.3</title>
      <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:52:14 GMT</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>171</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.4.3</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>13.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description>&lt;h3&gt;Jean 0.4.3&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;**Updates install themselves.** From now on Jean checks every hour, installs updates and relaunches by itself.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;**The hub on your phone (setup).** `jean tunnel setup` connects the hub to your own address behind Cloudflare sign-in, from one paste.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;**Fewer false stops.** The guard no longer blocks read-only commands like awk, find and git branch --list, or notes that name a file. Real risks still need your check mark.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;**Your plan, never an API key.** Lanes, relays and Studio never pick up an Anthropic API key from the Mac, so Jean always bills your Claude plan.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;**Dev bench (off by default).** A nightly review of the lanes work, for Jeans developers.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/msiegerJBI/jean-updates/releases/download/v0.4.3/Jean.dmg" length="140389700" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="oUsXRQV2yESmYsNDVLHLHVusID6fIZ586RvI0cb3iCXAQZ8S4kdk92HBqBpVWj+1GWenil8/RG+FFpsj9r3DDg==" />
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Jean 0.4.2</title>
      <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:08:12 GMT</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>147</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.4.2</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>13.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description>&lt;h3&gt;Jean 0.4.2&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Slack works again: 0.4.1 stopped Jean from hearing messages, check marks and Approve/Deny buttons. Anything you sent in Slack since updating to 0.4.1, please send again.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/msiegerJBI/jean-updates/releases/download/v0.4.2/Jean.dmg" length="140322145" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="WqLPEvDAXZM2MOefPWzUQ4sHX/P6oiyaQWbzqVLIg35NOra1HHnxvD5FgJ/LZcU6NpAkZQQCGadbAJO9TjbOBA==" />
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Jean 0.4.1</title>
      <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:52:10 GMT</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>145</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.4.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>13.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description>&lt;h3&gt;Jean 0.4.1&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;**Tidier Slack threads** - Send several messages in a row and Jean answers them together, once. - A "thanks" or "all good" gets a 👍 instead of a reply. - Each request ends as one message: the "On it" card turns into the answer. - Shorter answers, no repeated commands, and a new topic gets its own thread.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;**Studio message queue** - Type while Studio is working: your message joins the task in progress. - If the task has just finished, it waits and runs next. Stop hands it back.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/msiegerJBI/jean-updates/releases/download/v0.4.1/Jean.dmg" length="140265493" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="Qt31XMatk+J1H8BTQx3abz0FuhdHXY9mzy3hm1oogLE/W+lm/Y7mtD4CK7XZitPxUenGMAUh69AxmFt8Pm+ZDA==" />
    </item>
